   "name": "Chlorophyll in Photosynthesis",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Chlorophyll in Photosynthesis"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Chlorophyll is a **green pigment** that is present inside plant cells\n\n  - Chlorophyll reflects green light and so gives plants their characteristic green colour\n- Chlorophyll is found within **chloroplasts**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2023/10/chloroplast-micrograph.jpg",
   "file": "assets/7f2a0a6302aa-chloroplast-micrograph.jpg",
   "alt": "chloroplast-micrograph",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "*Kelvinsong, CC BY 3.0, via **[Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moss_chloroplasts_100%C3%97_objective.jpg)*"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Chlorophyll can be seen within chloroplasts under a light microscope***"
  },
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_Y5B3KYcxbh34tR49",
   "name": "Chlorophyll in Photosynthesis: Extended",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Chlorophyll in Photosynthesis: Extended"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Extended Tier Only"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis is to absorb light energy\n- Chlorophyll **transfers this light energy into chemical energy** during the synthesis of **carbohydrates**\n\n  - Glucose is an example of a carbohydrate that contains stored chemical energy"
  }
